#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1818
msgid "Browser Filter"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:928
msgid ""
"Show clicks only from specific browsers like Chrome, Firefox, or Safari. "
"Helps identify browser-specific behavior patterns."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:929
msgid "Show clicks from people using certain web browsers."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:932
#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1830
msgid "Visitor Type Filter"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:933
msgid ""
"Filter between logged-in users and guest visitors. Logged-in users often "
"behave differently because they're more familiar with your site."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:934
msgid "Show clicks from logged-in users only, guests only, or everyone."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:940
msgid ""
"View the heatmap rendered from desktop computer users. The number on this "
"chip is the distinct human, spam-excluded desktop sessions MATCHING your "
"currently applied filters — same canonical universe as the header Sessions "
"count, so the desktop, mobile, and tablet chips add up to the filtered total"
" (which equals the header Sessions pill when no advanced filter is applied)."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:941
msgid ""
"Desktop heatmap. The number is real desktop sessions matching your current "
"filters; the three device chips add up to the filtered total."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:945
msgid ""
"View the heatmap rendered from mobile phone users. The number on this chip "
"is the distinct human, spam-excluded mobile sessions MATCHING your currently"
" applied filters — same canonical universe as the header Sessions count, so "
"the desktop, mobile, and tablet chips add up to the filtered total (which "
"equals the header Sessions pill when no advanced filter is applied)."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:946
msgid ""
"Mobile heatmap. The number is real mobile sessions matching your current "
"filters; the three device chips add up to the filtered total."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:949
msgid "Tablet View"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:950
msgid ""
"View the heatmap rendered from tablet users. The number on this chip is the "
"distinct human, spam-excluded tablet sessions MATCHING your currently "
"applied filters — same canonical universe as the header Sessions count, so "
"the desktop, mobile, and tablet chips add up to the filtered total (which "
"equals the header Sessions pill when no advanced filter is applied)."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:951
msgid ""
"Tablet heatmap. The number is real tablet sessions matching your current "
"filters; the three device chips add up to the filtered total."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:958
msgid "A color map showing where people click the most."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:963
msgid "Shows where people move their mouse."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:968
msgid "Shows which parts people look at most."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:973
msgid "Shows how far down people scroll."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:979
msgid ""
"Total number of times this page was viewed during the selected period. Each "
